==Albanian==

===Alternative forms===
* [[dirsë]] (Gheg)

===Etymology===
Probably s-formation from {{term|djerr|lang=sq}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|sq}} {{term/t|ine-pro|*ters-||dry}}, cognate to Ancient Greek {{term|τέρσομαι|tr=tersomai|lang=grc|sc=polytonic}}, Sanskrit {{term|तृष्यति|sc=Deva|tr=tṛṣyati|lang=sa}}, Old English {{term|þurst|lang=ang}} and Latin {{term|terra|lang=la}}. Alternatively from {{etyl|sqj-pro|sq}} {{term/t|sqj-pro|*widertjā}}, from {{term/t|sqj-pro|*swidertjā}}, from pre-Albanian {{term/t|ine-pro|*swidrotyeh₂}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|sq}} {{term/t|ine-pro|*sweyd-}} (compare Greek {{term|ιδρός|tr=idrós|lang=el}}, English {{term|sweat|lang=en}}, Italian {{term|sudore|lang=it}})<ref>A Concise Historical Grammar of the Albanian Language, V.Orel, Koninklijke Brill , Leiden 2000</ref>.

